1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,009
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:07,009 --> 00:00:10,805
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,805 --> 00:00:12,996
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:12,996 --> 00:00:14,206
I just lost a Sports Day match.

5
00:00:14,329 --> 00:00:15,320
You don’t have to comfort me.

6
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,109
Free hugs.

7
00:00:16,109 --> 00:00:18,320
You're the best in my eyes, P’Niran.

8
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,547
Did you lose a Sports Day match today?

9
00:00:19,547 --> 00:00:21,293
What did Coach Ong call to tell you this time?

10
00:00:21,293 --> 00:00:22,063
What are you looking at?

11
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:23,469
Haven’t you ever seen a 12th-grader cry?

12
00:00:23,469 --> 00:00:24,744
I’m sorry.

13
00:00:25,065 --> 00:00:27,266
I let you cry for so long.

14
00:00:27,389 --> 00:00:29,891
I want to be by your side at a time like this.

15
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,345
Today, I’m going to be that planet

16
00:00:32,641 --> 00:00:34,697
that helps absorb your tears.

17
00:00:34,894 --> 00:00:37,179
Let this planet be flooded.

18
00:00:37,179 --> 00:00:38,802
We’ll float together.

19
00:01:40,345 --> 00:01:41,717
You have stars in your room.

20
00:01:44,481 --> 00:01:47,086
My dad made them for me when I was a kid.

21
00:01:48,666 --> 00:01:49,538
That’s great.

22
00:01:50,723 --> 00:01:52,374
Your dad is so sweet.

23
00:01:55,286 --> 00:01:57,668
I have some more stars like that.

24
00:01:58,458 --> 00:01:59,969
If you like them,

25
00:02:00,932 --> 00:02:03,776
you can put them up in your room too.

26
00:02:08,441 --> 00:02:09,685
Do you have a headache?

27
00:02:12,474 --> 00:02:13,379
Why would I?

28
00:02:14,243 --> 00:02:16,893
I just cried. I’m not sick.

29
00:02:18,176 --> 00:02:21,432
Most people get headaches when they cry.

30
00:02:29,133 --> 00:02:31,537
Cheewa, are you really single?

31
00:02:32,894 --> 00:02:36,164
I’m single. Why do you ask?

32
00:02:38,114 --> 00:02:39,027
Well…

33
00:02:42,803 --> 00:02:44,806
You seem to take good care of people.

34
00:02:47,003 --> 00:02:48,756
Have you been like this
since you were a kid?

35
00:02:50,632 --> 00:02:55,053
Well, my parents take care of me like this.

36
00:02:58,163 --> 00:03:00,264
Are you saying you’re my parents?

37
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,043
No.

38
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:07,511
I’m just saying my parents
take care of me like this

39
00:03:07,758 --> 00:03:09,914
because they love me
and want the best for me.

40
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:15,529
When I love someone and want the best
for them, I want to take care of them too.

41
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,458
Hey, Cheewa.

42
00:03:31,878 --> 00:03:32,522
Yes?

43
00:03:35,163 --> 00:03:36,585
Can I sleep here tonight?

44
00:03:36,931 --> 00:03:38,630
I don’t want to go home and see my dad yet.

45
00:03:40,037 --> 00:03:41,018
Of course.

46
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,708
You can stay for as long as you like.

47
00:03:45,411 --> 00:03:46,848
As long as I like?

48
00:03:47,218 --> 00:03:48,664
You can stay for eternity.

49
00:03:49,256 --> 00:03:52,957
♪ I can feel it too ♪

50
00:03:55,376 --> 00:04:00,238
♪ There’s someone to see me through ♪

51
00:04:00,238 --> 00:04:02,932
♪ I have nothing to fear ♪

52
00:04:02,932 --> 00:04:05,571
♪ Because I hold you dear ♪

53
00:04:05,571 --> 00:04:10,793
♪ I always feel safe here ♪

54
00:04:11,509 --> 00:04:13,498
I want to take a shower.

55
00:04:13,844 --> 00:04:14,789
Can I borrow your clothes?

56
00:04:15,357 --> 00:04:16,207
Sure.

57
00:04:16,429 --> 00:04:18,024
Give me a second.

58
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:23,525
Wait, do you mind if I sleep in your bed?

59
00:04:23,895 --> 00:04:25,211
Make yourself at home.

60
00:04:34,321 --> 00:04:35,293
Do you know them?

61
00:04:36,914 --> 00:04:37,920
Are they a boyband?

62
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,140
Yeah, I think so.

63
00:04:39,338 --> 00:04:40,290
I love them so much.

64
00:04:40,290 --> 00:04:41,903
I’ve seen them. They’re handsome.

65
00:04:41,903 --> 00:04:42,694
Who’s the most handsome?

66
00:04:42,694 --> 00:04:43,408
Hey!

67
00:04:43,704 --> 00:04:45,302
You and I need to talk.

68
00:04:51,645 --> 00:04:55,456
Following Mr. Oy from the Boxing Club
being bullied by an unseen entity,

69
00:04:55,456 --> 00:04:58,057
information was circulated
throughout the school

70
00:04:58,057 --> 00:04:59,880
that it was the doing of
the science building’s ghost.

71
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:04,178
Initially, Mr. Oy has accused Mr. Niran
from the Judo Club of being behind it,

72
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:07,220
forcing us from the Astronomy Club,
known as the Universe Court,

73
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:08,912
to step in and urgently find a solution
to this situation.

74
00:05:08,912 --> 00:05:10,024
You call this urgent?

75
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:11,456
They nearly beat each other to death.

76
00:05:12,394 --> 00:05:14,054
Is he obsessed with Judge Bao
or something?

77
00:05:15,535 --> 00:05:16,546
No idea.

78
00:05:16,719 --> 00:05:18,840
Since neither side has any evidence
to prove their case,

79
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:20,655
we have to hold a hearing today.

80
00:05:22,432 --> 00:05:24,068
What the hell is wrong with you now, Oy?

81
00:05:25,277 --> 00:05:26,808
I want to end this already.

82
00:05:27,376 --> 00:05:31,281
At first, it just annoyed me,
but now it’s affecting my life.

83
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:32,870
I get bullied every day.

84
00:05:34,005 --> 00:05:35,222
You have to prove it.

85
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:38,403
And get the science building kids
to help.

86
00:05:39,884 --> 00:05:42,461
So my friend is being accused of
being the culprit?

87
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:44,835
Do you have evidence that my friend did it?

88
00:05:47,575 --> 00:05:48,431
I don’t.

89
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:51,061
You don’t have any evidence,
but you won’t stop accusing him?

90
00:05:51,357 --> 00:05:53,026
If it’s not your friend, who could it be?

91
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,193
There’s no one else.

92
00:05:56,945 --> 00:05:58,557
You say that a lot.

93
00:05:58,779 --> 00:06:00,795
It’s ridiculous, you know?

94
00:06:00,997 --> 00:06:03,008
Even a kindergarten kid
is more reasonable than you.

95
00:06:04,119 --> 00:06:04,846
Yeah.

96
00:06:05,241 --> 00:06:06,561
Even though I’m stupid,

97
00:06:07,326 --> 00:06:08,886
I can still think better than you.

98
00:06:09,232 --> 00:06:10,304
And my friend is stupid.

99
00:06:10,304 --> 00:06:10,935
Excuse me?

100
00:06:10,935 --> 00:06:11,520
Hey!

101
00:06:11,668 --> 00:06:13,906
You saw me come alone,
so you're ganging up on me, assholes?

102
00:06:14,079 --> 00:06:14,991
Exactly.

103
00:06:15,707 --> 00:06:18,650
If you came with more people,
how could I fight you?

104
00:06:20,699 --> 00:06:22,178
Stop arguing already.

105
00:06:22,375 --> 00:06:23,699
It’s such a waste of time.

106
00:06:24,242 --> 00:06:26,087
P’Niran, you really didn’t do it, did you?

107
00:06:26,087 --> 00:06:27,541
You’re sure?

108
00:06:27,541 --> 00:06:28,344
Of course.

109
00:06:28,912 --> 00:06:30,773
Can you swear to it?

110
00:06:30,970 --> 00:06:31,922
Are you really a science kid?

111
00:06:31,922 --> 00:06:32,953
Why are you making me swear?

112
00:06:33,150 --> 00:06:34,041
Come on.

113
00:06:34,041 --> 00:06:35,052
Just swear.

114
00:06:35,052 --> 00:06:36,562
Swear before the universe.

115
00:06:36,685 --> 00:06:38,159
It’s greater than anything else.

116
00:06:39,911 --> 00:06:41,249
Nonsense.

117
00:06:41,471 --> 00:06:43,228
My friend isn’t going to do anything that silly.

118
00:06:43,228 --> 00:06:43,947
Yeah.

119
00:06:44,144 --> 00:06:45,267
If I did it,

120
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:49,546
I hope I fail my exams, have to repeat
a year, can’t go to university,

121
00:06:49,546 --> 00:06:51,155
and get stuck here for another year.

122
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:52,125
Sadhu!

123
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,244
Great. You can be stuck with Cheewa
for another year.

124
00:06:58,786 --> 00:07:01,579
Have you ever told the teachers about this?

125
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:02,970
Your mom is a teacher.

126
00:07:03,488 --> 00:07:04,804
Have you tried telling her?

127
00:07:05,742 --> 00:07:07,101
My mom won’t believe me.

128
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,544
I’m not good enough in her eyes.

129
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,808
I’m a piece of shit.

130
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,461
That’s true.

131
00:07:16,731 --> 00:07:19,612
I guess I’ll have to get beaten to death
before she believes me

132
00:07:19,612 --> 00:07:21,179
Please don’t talk like that.

133
00:07:21,599 --> 00:07:24,159
Let’s just talk about catching the culprit.

134
00:07:24,899 --> 00:07:26,565
Fine. I’m just complaining.

135
00:07:26,565 --> 00:07:27,613
Why are you taking it so seriously?

136
00:07:28,995 --> 00:07:29,996
How about this?

137
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:32,721
Since Oy couldn’t find any evidence
to accuse me,

138
00:07:33,165 --> 00:07:36,603
I’ll find evidence myself
to prove that I’m not the bad guy.

139
00:07:37,911 --> 00:07:38,569
That’s it.

140
00:07:40,025 --> 00:07:41,415
How will you proceed?

141
00:07:41,415 --> 00:07:42,903
I’ll track down the real culprit, of course.

142
00:07:45,001 --> 00:07:46,952
But what if the real culprit is a ghost?

143
00:07:47,396 --> 00:07:49,171
We have to look for a ghost?

144
00:07:49,961 --> 00:07:50,746
Hem.

145
00:07:51,388 --> 00:07:52,253
Listen to me.

146
00:07:52,771 --> 00:07:53,672
Don’t be delusional.

147
00:07:54,264 --> 00:07:55,987
Ugh. Ghostbusters.

148
00:07:56,727 --> 00:07:58,380
I can’t with my friends.

149
00:08:01,219 --> 00:08:02,110
I have a plan.

150
00:08:05,713 --> 00:08:06,806
P’Niran.

151
00:08:07,349 --> 00:08:07,910
Hmm?

152
00:08:09,169 --> 00:08:10,706
Are you sure you’re okay?

153
00:08:11,743 --> 00:08:12,643
About what?

154
00:08:13,457 --> 00:08:15,005
About what P’Oy said in the club room.

155
00:08:17,448 --> 00:08:19,093
Oh, I’m fine.

156
00:08:19,093 --> 00:08:20,244
I get him.

157
00:08:20,985 --> 00:08:22,963
Just his words can't make me
think anything bad.

158
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,153
Are you worried about me?

159
00:08:32,288 --> 00:08:33,039
Yes.

160
00:08:34,569 --> 00:08:35,638
Why are you worried about me?

161
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,841
If I don’t worry about you,
who am I supposed to worry about?

162
00:08:42,346 --> 00:08:43,698
I like you.

163
00:08:52,875 --> 00:08:53,541
Stop it.

164
00:08:53,541 --> 00:08:54,439
Go home.

165
00:08:55,846 --> 00:08:56,461
Are you coming?

166
00:08:56,461 --> 00:08:57,563
It’s about to rain.

167
00:08:57,810 --> 00:08:59,129
I have an umbrella.

168
00:08:59,129 --> 00:09:00,241
No need for an umbrella. Run!

169
00:09:00,241 --> 00:09:01,280
Come on!

170
00:09:02,736 --> 00:09:03,566
Oh, Glasses.

171
00:09:11,654 --> 00:09:13,484
Did your mom already give you
her wedding invite?

172
00:09:26,785 --> 00:09:27,537
Um…

173
00:09:28,647 --> 00:09:33,519
Dress nicely. Find something nice
to wear to her wedding.

174
00:09:42,695 --> 00:09:43,735
I’m not going.

175
00:09:45,635 --> 00:09:47,479
How could you not go?

176
00:09:47,652 --> 00:09:49,045
She’s your mom.

177
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:54,984
I don’t want to go.

178
00:09:55,527 --> 00:09:56,947
Come on.

179
00:09:57,539 --> 00:09:59,098
Don’t act like a child.

180
00:09:59,271 --> 00:10:01,052
You’re a grown-up.

181
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:03,533
Your mom is getting married.

182
00:10:03,928 --> 00:10:06,005
Go congratulate her.

183
00:10:07,979 --> 00:10:09,486
At least go out of courtesy.

184
00:10:15,804 --> 00:10:17,085
If you’re happy for her, you go.

185
00:10:19,109 --> 00:10:20,408
I’m not happy.

186
00:10:20,852 --> 00:10:21,756
I’m not going.

187
00:11:06,530 --> 00:11:08,076
Damn it.

188
00:11:08,076 --> 00:11:10,090
Why does this have to happen to me?

189
00:11:54,692 --> 00:11:55,830
You can’t sleep?

190
00:11:58,101 --> 00:12:00,306
Yeah, I’m a little frustrated.

191
00:12:04,205 --> 00:12:05,574
Is something wrong?

192
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:08,145
(You can tell me.)

193
00:12:09,749 --> 00:12:12,217
I don’t know how to explain.

194
00:12:15,302 --> 00:12:17,169
Can you just stay still

195
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:20,240
and let me hear your voice?

196
00:13:39,778 --> 00:13:41,008
(Is that any good?)

197
00:13:41,304 --> 00:13:42,733
(I’ve been practicing this song.)

198
00:13:43,177 --> 00:13:43,790
Huh?

199
00:13:46,307 --> 00:13:47,347
What did you ask again?

200
00:13:48,853 --> 00:13:49,902
P’Niran,

201
00:13:52,814 --> 00:13:54,072
I asked if you liked it.

202
00:14:00,144 --> 00:14:00,968
Um…

203
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,059
I do.

204
00:14:09,561 --> 00:14:10,240
Yeah.

205
00:14:11,326 --> 00:14:12,731
So do I.

206
00:14:19,025 --> 00:14:20,183
(P’Niran.)

207
00:14:21,837 --> 00:14:22,603
Yes?

208
00:14:28,599 --> 00:14:33,506
I meant what I said the other night.

209
00:14:44,894 --> 00:14:46,352
What a great service.

210
00:14:46,662 --> 00:14:48,079
Do I have to pay for staying over?

211
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,774
Feel free to pay with your heart.

212
00:14:54,698 --> 00:14:55,750
Cheewa,

213
00:14:57,206 --> 00:14:59,341
are you this straightforward
about everything?

214
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,360
Don’t you get shy at all?

215
00:15:03,779 --> 00:15:04,626
I am.

216
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,429
Do I make you uncomfortable?

217
00:15:09,514 --> 00:15:10,255
No.

218
00:15:12,106 --> 00:15:13,872
I actually respect you for it.

219
00:15:14,653 --> 00:15:16,613
You’re not afraid to speak your mind.

220
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:19,407
I’ve never seen you beat around the bush.

221
00:15:21,505 --> 00:15:22,470
Did you know?

222
00:15:23,877 --> 00:15:26,935
The average human lifespan is 78.1 years.

223
00:15:27,675 --> 00:15:29,413
If you keep beating around the bush,

224
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:34,371
it’s like you lose
20% of your life.

225
00:15:34,717 --> 00:15:36,131
Oh…

226
00:15:39,883 --> 00:15:41,083
20%?

227
00:15:42,638 --> 00:15:46,739
So there’s 60-something years left?

228
00:15:46,739 --> 00:15:48,364
62.5 years.

229
00:15:48,858 --> 00:15:50,272
Okay. I give up.

230
00:15:51,111 --> 00:15:52,721
Nong Cheewa is always right.

231
00:15:53,881 --> 00:15:54,914
Next time,

232
00:15:54,914 --> 00:15:57,763
you can be straightforward with P’Niran.

233
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,574
P’Niran gets it now.

234
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,708
I can be straightforward
about everything, right?

235
00:16:05,115 --> 00:16:05,784
Yes.

236
00:16:14,228 --> 00:16:15,956
I like you, P’Niran.

237
00:16:16,524 --> 00:16:17,832
I really do.

238
00:16:43,819 --> 00:16:44,550
Cheewa,

239
00:16:47,709 --> 00:16:51,642
do you know what I asked my mom
the day she was about to leave me?

240
00:16:56,282 --> 00:17:02,062
I asked how much I had to love her
for her to stay with me.

241
00:17:08,405 --> 00:17:09,919
How much I had to love her

242
00:17:12,436 --> 00:17:13,653
for her not to leave me.

243
00:17:16,936 --> 00:17:18,958
I’d love her that much.

244
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:33,435
But in the end, she’s still gone.

245
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,305
Even though I love her that much,

246
00:17:43,044 --> 00:17:44,332
she still left me.

247
00:17:52,236 --> 00:17:53,743
Do you understand me, Cheewa?

248
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:58,417
Everyone I love

249
00:18:08,166 --> 00:18:09,569
might all be gone.

250
00:18:19,136 --> 00:18:20,969
Please understand me, Cheewa.

251
00:18:23,314 --> 00:18:25,098
I might need some time,

252
00:18:26,579 --> 00:18:28,192
but I’m really trying

253
00:18:30,611 --> 00:18:32,155
to work through a lot of things.

254
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,579
Take as much time as you need, P’Niran.

255
00:18:40,948 --> 00:18:42,941
But that whole time,

256
00:18:44,718 --> 00:18:46,301
(I’ll be right here for you.)

257
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:11,061
Please let me go with you.

258
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,450
I’m worried about you.

259
00:19:14,967 --> 00:19:17,195
If something happens, I can protect you.

260
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,655
The Universe Court
has come to the conclusion

261
00:19:31,655 --> 00:19:35,692
that Mr. Niran from the Judo Club can prove
his innocence by finding the real culprit.

262
00:19:36,046 --> 00:19:36,801
Hmm?

263
00:19:37,412 --> 00:19:39,866
The accused has to
prove his own innocence?

264
00:19:39,962 --> 00:19:40,999
What kind of court is that?

265
00:19:42,992 --> 00:19:46,429
What do you say, P’Niran?

266
00:19:47,651 --> 00:19:48,660
Boxing Club.

267
00:19:49,126 --> 00:19:51,550
I think the one who bullied him
is someone close to him.

268
00:19:52,273 --> 00:19:53,329
You guys have to help me.

269
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,173
You’re way off.

270
00:19:55,799 --> 00:19:58,071
It’s my club. Who would dare bully me?

271
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:00,057
Thara,

272
00:20:01,150 --> 00:20:03,314
go pretend to work out in their area
and keep an eye out for me.

273
00:20:11,268 --> 00:20:11,999
Thipok,

274
00:20:12,369 --> 00:20:14,266
go join the Boxing Club.

275
00:20:25,024 --> 00:20:26,080
Will that be convincing?

276
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:29,419
What if they catch on
that I have an ulterior motive?

277
00:20:29,499 --> 00:20:31,586
What if I get beaten up by their coach?

278
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:34,135
You won’t.

279
00:20:37,558 --> 00:20:39,728
This is our special coach.

280
00:20:39,728 --> 00:20:40,542
Coach Henry.

281
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:41,315
Yeah.

282
00:20:41,492 --> 00:20:42,285
Hello.

283
00:20:42,381 --> 00:20:43,789
My name is Henry.

284
00:20:44,721 --> 00:20:45,473
What about you?

285
00:20:45,891 --> 00:20:46,708
What are you going to do?

286
00:20:47,319 --> 00:20:47,988
Me?

287
00:20:48,904 --> 00:20:50,324
I’m going to observe from the outside.

288
00:20:50,629 --> 00:20:52,063
Too many people in there
will make things messy and blow our plan.

289
00:20:52,304 --> 00:20:54,416
Yeah. Easy for you to say.

290
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:56,691
We’re the ones who have to
play these random roles.

291
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:01,110
I think that’ll be a waste of time.

292
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:02,522
Let’s go with another plan.

293
00:21:02,779 --> 00:21:06,619
But I think there’s a reason
the culprit is someone from your circle.

294
00:21:07,197 --> 00:21:08,418
Like P’Niran said.

295
00:21:09,993 --> 00:21:11,218
Because Oy is…

296
00:21:12,889 --> 00:21:13,423
What?

297
00:21:13,423 --> 00:21:14,279
Cover your ears for a second.

298
00:21:15,709 --> 00:21:16,428
Cover your ears.

299
00:21:18,790 --> 00:21:19,493
Yeah.

300
00:21:19,927 --> 00:21:22,404
Oy talks so much shit
and has a shitty personality.

301
00:21:22,404 --> 00:21:24,245
He’s so unlikeable.

302
00:21:24,245 --> 00:21:25,384
And he still has the nerve to insist

303
00:21:25,384 --> 00:21:26,350
that no one would dare
make an enemy of him.

304
00:21:26,656 --> 00:21:28,156
So it has to be someone close to him.

305
00:21:28,413 --> 00:21:29,786
Who the hell could stay close to him?

306
00:21:29,786 --> 00:21:31,646
Just being around him is freaking annoying.

307
00:21:31,646 --> 00:21:32,396
Damn.

308
00:21:32,396 --> 00:21:34,136
Not to mention how he looks.

309
00:21:34,136 --> 00:21:34,808
Are you done?

310
00:21:34,808 --> 00:21:35,308
Yeah.

311
00:21:35,308 --> 00:21:36,403
I’m done.

312
00:21:38,171 --> 00:21:41,284
I’ll stay with you, P’Niran.

313
00:21:42,393 --> 00:21:43,363
You don’t have to.

314
00:21:43,363 --> 00:21:44,986
You can stand by with your friends.

315
00:21:44,986 --> 00:21:47,103
Once I catch the culprit,
Jomyut can interrogate them.

316
00:21:48,437 --> 00:21:49,927
Please let me go with you.

317
00:21:50,409 --> 00:21:51,196
I’m worried about you.

318
00:21:55,262 --> 00:21:57,066
If something happens, I can protect you.

319
00:21:59,862 --> 00:22:01,313
Who’s protecting who?

320
00:22:05,509 --> 00:22:07,470
Henry!

321
00:22:07,631 --> 00:22:08,649
Let’s go push up!

322
00:22:08,649 --> 00:22:14,044
Henry!

323
00:22:16,053 --> 00:22:17,088
Do you think they’ll pull it off?

324
00:22:18,598 --> 00:22:19,098
Of course, they will.

325
00:22:21,444 --> 00:22:22,001
Come on.

326
00:22:23,029 --> 00:22:24,682
Did you make them do this on purpose?

327
00:22:25,775 --> 00:22:26,460
No.

328
00:22:29,513 --> 00:22:31,067
Let’s focus on catching the culprit.

329
00:22:31,598 --> 00:22:32,254
Yeah.

330
00:22:35,263 --> 00:22:36,198
He’s so weird.

331
00:22:37,307 --> 00:22:37,807
Yeah.

332
00:22:46,195 --> 00:22:48,058
Yeah, Oy is being crazy again.

333
00:22:48,187 --> 00:22:49,994
All he does is pick on Niran.

334
00:22:50,091 --> 00:22:51,379
It’s freaking hilarious.

335
00:22:53,275 --> 00:22:55,561
Yeah, and he thinks Niran did it.

336
00:22:55,561 --> 00:22:56,648
I’m losing it.

337
00:22:59,589 --> 00:23:02,139
But does he not suspect you at all?

338
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:03,377
Not at all.

339
00:23:03,634 --> 00:23:04,821
He’s freaking stupid.

340
00:23:04,950 --> 00:23:06,476
Wanna go to the bathroom?

341
00:23:06,476 --> 00:23:07,030
Yeah.

342
00:23:08,268 --> 00:23:08,816
Come on!

343
00:23:13,203 --> 00:23:13,913
Are they gone?

344
00:23:15,038 --> 00:23:15,795
Not yet.

345
00:23:16,454 --> 00:23:17,358
Are they gone?

346
00:23:18,290 --> 00:23:19,104
Can I get up now?

347
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:21,198
I don’t think they are.

348
00:23:22,660 --> 00:23:23,371
Really?

349
00:23:24,296 --> 00:23:24,950
Are they gone?

350
00:23:26,171 --> 00:23:27,934
I think we should keep hiding like this.

351
00:23:27,934 --> 00:23:28,999
It’s safer.

352
00:23:29,883 --> 00:23:30,698
I don’t think so.

353
00:23:40,984 --> 00:23:41,729
Let’s go.

354
00:23:42,691 --> 00:23:43,802
I’m so damn hungry.

355
00:23:43,963 --> 00:23:44,863
What are you guys eating?

356
00:23:45,297 --> 00:23:45,990
No idea.

357
00:23:46,134 --> 00:23:46,852
You pick.

358
00:23:47,238 --> 00:23:48,425
I’ve picked enough.

359
00:23:48,425 --> 00:23:49,364
Crispy pork basil.

360
00:23:49,701 --> 00:23:50,425
No, noodles.

361
00:23:50,425 --> 00:23:50,925
Again?

362
00:23:51,358 --> 00:23:52,198
Noodles? Please.

363
00:23:52,310 --> 00:23:53,573
You two eat that shit all the time.

364
00:23:55,743 --> 00:23:56,243
Again?

365
00:23:56,789 --> 00:23:58,288
You two pay.

366
00:23:58,850 --> 00:24:00,377
Oh, look what I’m wearing.

367
00:24:00,377 --> 00:24:01,018
You want me to pay?

368
00:24:01,114 --> 00:24:01,945
I don’t have any money.

369
00:24:01,945 --> 00:24:02,909
It’s Naw.

370
00:24:03,246 --> 00:24:04,125
Come on.

371
00:24:04,205 --> 00:24:05,852
I don’t have anything to do with this.

372
00:24:17,293 --> 00:24:18,051
Hey!

373
00:24:18,517 --> 00:24:19,319
Let go!

374
00:24:19,977 --> 00:24:21,032
What the hell are you guys doing?

375
00:24:21,869 --> 00:24:22,955
Shut up!

376
00:24:23,421 --> 00:24:24,514
What the hell are you guys doing?

377
00:24:25,767 --> 00:24:26,777
Please.

378
00:24:27,195 --> 00:24:29,360
Turn on the lights
and stop shining that on my face already.

379
00:24:29,955 --> 00:24:30,915
My eyes sting.

380
00:24:31,124 --> 00:24:31,909
No!

381
00:24:33,323 --> 00:24:34,587
Just confess.

382
00:24:34,587 --> 00:24:35,851
You’ll get a lighter sentence.

383
00:24:36,831 --> 00:24:37,595
Confess?

384
00:24:38,463 --> 00:24:39,189
About what?

385
00:24:40,153 --> 00:24:41,323
You guys haven’t told me anything.

386
00:24:41,500 --> 00:24:42,368
Are you idiots?

387
00:24:46,482 --> 00:24:47,216
About me.

388
00:24:48,759 --> 00:24:49,259
Oh.

389
00:24:49,805 --> 00:24:50,485
Hey, Oy.

390
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:53,004
Why are you with them?

391
00:24:54,241 --> 00:24:55,318
Is there something you want to tell me?

392
00:25:02,066 --> 00:25:02,742
Tell you what?

393
00:25:03,594 --> 00:25:04,966
Let’s go back to our club.

394
00:25:10,731 --> 00:25:11,545
Most of the time,

395
00:25:11,706 --> 00:25:13,251
Oy gets bullied
when he passes the science building.

396
00:25:14,167 --> 00:25:15,641
So we have to lure them
to the science building.

397
00:25:16,107 --> 00:25:17,039
Your job

398
00:25:17,296 --> 00:25:19,919
is to pretend you don’t know you got caught
and drag them over here.

399
00:25:21,622 --> 00:25:22,754
What the hell are you talking about?

400
00:25:23,863 --> 00:25:25,108
You do know

401
00:25:25,300 --> 00:25:26,910
that P’Oy has been bullied this whole time

402
00:25:27,167 --> 00:25:29,106
and he blames P’Niran for it.

403
00:25:29,701 --> 00:25:30,888
Today,

404
00:25:31,965 --> 00:25:33,937
we heard you talk to your friends
from your club.

405
00:25:39,609 --> 00:25:40,299
About what?

406
00:25:43,245 --> 00:25:44,530
If you’ve got something to say,
just f*cking tell me.

407
00:25:44,964 --> 00:25:47,748
If you really have nothing to do with this,
I’ll beat the shit out of them.

408
00:25:48,439 --> 00:25:49,095
Excuse me?

409
00:25:50,638 --> 00:25:52,210
So much for helping you.

410
00:26:01,709 --> 00:26:04,902
Well, Oy likes to put people down in the club.

411
00:26:10,189 --> 00:26:11,475
You have to own up to it, man.

412
00:26:13,709 --> 00:26:14,767
You really do that.

413
00:26:16,278 --> 00:26:18,148
You’ve gotten on everyone’s nerves
in the club.

414
00:26:24,644 --> 00:26:26,055
I’m going to catch them red-handed.

415
00:26:28,658 --> 00:26:29,818
Just tell us what to do.

416
00:26:33,450 --> 00:26:34,346
Here’s the plan.

417
00:26:34,571 --> 00:26:36,399
Oy, you’ll be the bait.

418
00:26:37,090 --> 00:26:38,025
And you, Naw.

419
00:26:38,395 --> 00:26:39,419
Go back to your gang

420
00:26:40,046 --> 00:26:41,464
and tell them to bully Oy again.

421
00:26:42,364 --> 00:26:43,085
As for you guys,

422
00:26:43,487 --> 00:26:45,452
record some evidence,
in case we need to send it to the teachers.

423
00:26:46,047 --> 00:26:46,915
Leave the rest to me.

424
00:26:48,988 --> 00:26:50,177
What about us?

425
00:26:51,205 --> 00:26:51,913
For you two,

426
00:26:52,733 --> 00:26:53,598
if they run,

427
00:26:54,434 --> 00:26:55,629
split up and spread out.

428
00:26:55,741 --> 00:26:56,602
Stop all of them.

429
00:26:57,068 --> 00:26:58,915
Everyone involved in this.

430
00:27:00,458 --> 00:27:01,651
Mission accepted.

431
00:27:02,679 --> 00:27:04,107
We won’t let you all down.

432
00:27:09,465 --> 00:27:10,818
You think you can pin this on me,

433
00:27:11,509 --> 00:27:12,633
you science building ghosts?

434
00:27:13,902 --> 00:27:15,806
You’re going to die in this building
all over again.

435
00:27:17,027 --> 00:27:18,051
No!

436
00:27:18,839 --> 00:27:19,829
I’m afraid of ghosts.

437
00:27:28,558 --> 00:27:30,588
Your hair smells nice too.

438
00:27:30,588 --> 00:27:32,450
And how could you smell someone’s hair
without asking?

439
00:27:32,627 --> 00:27:34,127
Next time, I’ll ask first.

440
00:27:34,127 --> 00:27:34,726
Oh.

441
00:27:34,726 --> 00:27:36,223
You cheeky kid.

442
00:27:36,448 --> 00:27:38,004
So you guys are the ones
pretending to be the science building ghosts.

443
00:27:49,062 --> 00:27:50,529
This time, I’ll leave him alone.

444
00:27:51,319 --> 00:27:52,650
I’ll join you guys.

445
00:27:54,099 --> 00:27:54,864
You sure?

446
00:27:54,864 --> 00:27:56,111
We can do it ourselves like usual.

447
00:27:56,111 --> 00:27:57,080
But I think that sounds fun.

448
00:27:57,754 --> 00:27:58,307
Yeah.

449
00:27:58,551 --> 00:28:00,269
This time, we can invite everyone.

450
00:28:00,878 --> 00:28:02,022
Anyone who hates that jerk.

451
00:28:02,730 --> 00:28:04,597
That’ll be too many people.

452
00:28:04,943 --> 00:28:06,501
The whole freaking club.

453
00:28:08,525 --> 00:28:10,253
Let’s go. What are we waiting for?

454
00:28:52,607 --> 00:28:53,978
How do we use this freaking camera?

455
00:28:55,426 --> 00:28:56,301
I don’t know.

456
00:28:56,416 --> 00:28:58,242
Why didn’t you ask Newton
when you took it?

457
00:28:59,081 --> 00:29:00,812
Shit, I forgot to ask him.

458
00:29:15,314 --> 00:29:16,693
Are you okay, P’Niran?

459
00:29:17,285 --> 00:29:18,813
It’s really dusty in here.

460
00:29:19,455 --> 00:29:21,396
Not to mention the smell of old books.

461
00:29:24,408 --> 00:29:25,659
I’m fine. No worries.

462
00:29:34,164 --> 00:29:34,669
Why?

463
00:29:35,673 --> 00:29:37,547
Do you want me to smell your shirt
like when we were at the Boxing Club?

464
00:29:39,802 --> 00:29:40,422
Do you want to?

465
00:29:40,521 --> 00:29:41,405
Oh.

466
00:29:41,405 --> 00:29:42,787
You cheeky kid.

467
00:29:44,005 --> 00:29:45,182
My shirt smells nice.

468
00:29:47,272 --> 00:29:48,484
I know it does.

469
00:29:48,994 --> 00:29:50,066
I was smelling it for a while.

470
00:29:52,584 --> 00:29:54,668
So you really do like this smell.

471
00:29:57,384 --> 00:29:58,012
What?

472
00:30:01,134 --> 00:30:03,178
Your hair smells nice too.

473
00:30:09,391 --> 00:30:11,325
I was wondering what was tickling my head.

474
00:30:11,325 --> 00:30:12,887
Turns out it was your nose.

475
00:30:14,072 --> 00:30:14,766
Yes.

476
00:30:14,989 --> 00:30:16,118
I was smelling it for a while.

477
00:30:17,682 --> 00:30:18,727
Hey, don’t get smart with me.

478
00:30:20,027 --> 00:30:21,836
And how could you smell someone’s hair
without asking?

479
00:30:22,659 --> 00:30:23,503
I’m sorry.

480
00:30:24,770 --> 00:30:26,599
Next time, I’ll ask first.

481
00:30:27,685 --> 00:30:28,446
What do you mean, next time?

482
00:30:38,105 --> 00:30:41,454
You two must’ve forgotten
that I’m sitting here too.

483
00:30:45,141 --> 00:30:46,814
When are Naw and the others coming?

484
00:30:46,871 --> 00:30:48,530
I want to get out of here.

485
00:30:50,242 --> 00:30:51,430
Are you hot?

486
00:30:53,158 --> 00:30:55,487
I’m sick of your love, Cheewa.

487
00:31:06,843 --> 00:31:07,616
Mm.

488
00:31:08,126 --> 00:31:09,731
He’s smiling at me, Hem.

489
00:31:10,027 --> 00:31:11,610
Go ahead and smell each other’s hair.

490
00:31:15,971 --> 00:31:19,064
Are you sure Oy is in there alone?

491
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:21,137
Yeah. He’s alone.

492
00:31:21,976 --> 00:31:23,049
Let’s f*cking get him.

493
00:31:23,049 --> 00:31:24,482
Let’s go.

494
00:31:24,795 --> 00:31:25,446
Let’s go.

495
00:31:27,896 --> 00:31:28,690
Go!

496
00:31:30,135 --> 00:31:31,176
Shit, they’re here.

497
00:31:32,303 --> 00:31:33,162
Hold on.

498
00:31:33,631 --> 00:31:34,398
We don’t want them to see us.

499
00:32:00,780 --> 00:32:01,893
Whoa!

500
00:32:04,551 --> 00:32:06,071
Shit, it’s vinegar?

501
00:32:06,795 --> 00:32:07,963
Ouch!

502
00:32:09,084 --> 00:32:10,052
Damn it!

503
00:32:10,480 --> 00:32:11,124
F*ck!

504
00:32:11,650 --> 00:32:12,321
Hey!

505
00:32:13,276 --> 00:32:15,737
Shit, open it!

506
00:32:16,434 --> 00:32:17,138
Hey!

507
00:32:18,498 --> 00:32:19,649
There’s way more of you than me.

508
00:32:19,649 --> 00:32:20,523
What’s there to be afraid of?

509
00:32:21,083 --> 00:32:22,302
What are you afraid of?

510
00:32:26,926 --> 00:32:28,204
Fight me one-on-one!

511
00:32:30,591 --> 00:32:31,637
Damn it!

512
00:32:48,135 --> 00:32:49,869
So you guys are the ones
pretending to be the science building ghosts.

513
00:32:51,004 --> 00:32:51,959
Shit, it’s Niran.

514
00:32:57,193 --> 00:32:58,220
Where do you think you’re going?

515
00:33:01,046 --> 00:33:02,465
Let’s go down the other side.

516
00:33:06,231 --> 00:33:07,653
Why the hell are you guys blocking us?

517
00:33:08,048 --> 00:33:09,326
Move, you four-eyes.

518
00:33:09,688 --> 00:33:10,548
Damn it.

519
00:33:14,284 --> 00:33:15,447
Did those assholes run away?

520
00:33:17,455 --> 00:33:18,256
Follow them.

521
00:33:18,256 --> 00:33:19,551
Don’t let them get away.

522
00:33:20,950 --> 00:33:22,792
But I need to get away from you right now.

523
00:33:23,302 --> 00:33:24,567
What the hell is that smell?

524
00:33:24,567 --> 00:33:25,501
Go take a shower.

525
00:33:29,133 --> 00:33:29,829
Shit.

526
00:33:33,533 --> 00:33:34,697
Hey! Why are you standing there smiling?

527
00:33:34,697 --> 00:33:35,379
Just go!

528
00:33:39,707 --> 00:33:41,290
You all have tainted
the science building’s reputation.

529
00:33:41,290 --> 00:33:42,393
You deserve to be punished.

530
00:33:43,265 --> 00:33:44,760
They’re over here, P’Niran!

531
00:33:44,831 --> 00:33:46,737
Why the hell did you tell him?

532
00:33:46,869 --> 00:33:47,698
Catch them!

533
00:34:13,394 --> 00:34:14,271
Close the door.

534
00:34:17,003 --> 00:34:18,300
There are so many of them.

535
00:34:18,448 --> 00:34:19,689
F*cking annoying.

536
00:34:20,890 --> 00:34:22,324
I’m so damn exhausted.

537
00:34:44,590 --> 00:34:45,853
It’s really you guys, huh?

538
00:34:47,104 --> 00:34:48,202
What the f*ck are you rambling about?

539
00:34:49,223 --> 00:34:51,492
Naw, go get the others.

540
00:34:53,302 --> 00:34:54,775
We’re going to f*ck them all up.

541
00:35:00,074 --> 00:35:01,208
Am I your friend?

542
00:35:05,325 --> 00:35:07,078
Someone who puts others beneath them

543
00:35:07,868 --> 00:35:09,390
isn’t someone we call a friend, Oy.

544
00:35:10,624 --> 00:35:12,424
You’re so mean you don’t even realize it.

545
00:35:12,967 --> 00:35:14,645
You f*cking piece of shit!

546
00:35:18,891 --> 00:35:21,466
Can’t you handle the fact
that nobody wants you?

547
00:35:23,631 --> 00:35:25,058
Nobody sees you as a friend.

548
00:35:42,311 --> 00:35:43,210
Are you done rambling?

549
00:35:44,938 --> 00:35:46,237
Let me punch you already.

550
00:35:46,431 --> 00:35:48,834
You’ve been pinning the blame on me
this whole time, asshole.

551
00:35:48,949 --> 00:35:50,199
P’Niran, don’t.

552
00:35:56,551 --> 00:35:57,632
I’ll deal with him for you.

553
00:36:00,391 --> 00:36:00,963
Asshole, aren’t you taking it too far?

554
00:36:00,963 --> 00:36:01,598
Hey!

555
00:36:01,927 --> 00:36:03,046
What are you guys doing?

556
00:36:12,109 --> 00:36:15,421
You don’t go to your judo practice,
but you have time to fight with other people.

557
00:36:15,421 --> 00:36:16,720
Aren’t you going to be good again?

558
00:36:19,111 --> 00:36:19,611
Hello.

559
00:36:19,611 --> 00:36:20,111
Oh—

560
00:36:20,111 --> 00:36:21,025
Where’s P’Niran?

561
00:36:32,834 --> 00:36:34,084
I’m afraid I can’t let him get away with it.

562
00:36:34,938 --> 00:36:39,119
Niran has been sent to the principal’s office
several times for the same reason.

563
00:36:39,914 --> 00:36:44,003
I’ll have to punish him
according to the school’s policy.

564
00:36:54,398 --> 00:36:55,197
I understand.

565
00:36:59,576 --> 00:37:01,680
I’d like to apologize to the school again.

566
00:37:18,331 --> 00:37:20,105
HUMAN RESOURCES DIVISION

567
00:37:20,237 --> 00:37:21,138
Hello.

568
00:37:26,629 --> 00:37:27,467
Let’s go home.

569
00:37:27,968 --> 00:37:29,295
Let me go get my bag first.

570
00:37:29,914 --> 00:37:30,590
Um…

571
00:37:52,705 --> 00:37:53,667
P’Niran!

572
00:38:00,723 --> 00:38:01,811
Go back to class, Cheewa.

573
00:38:03,548 --> 00:38:04,890
It’s not P’Niran’s fault.

574
00:38:04,890 --> 00:38:05,527
The whole thing happened because—

575
00:38:05,527 --> 00:38:06,027
It’s okay.

576
00:38:07,087 --> 00:38:08,319
Teacher Suchart told me everything.

577
00:38:14,044 --> 00:38:15,257
Go back to class, Cheewa.

578
00:38:16,744 --> 00:38:17,790
I got this.

579
00:38:53,718 --> 00:38:54,988
You don’t go to your judo practice,

580
00:38:55,974 --> 00:38:57,599
but you have time to fight with other people.

581
00:39:00,602 --> 00:39:01,868
Aren’t you embarrassed?

582
00:39:02,560 --> 00:39:03,060
Huh?

583
00:39:03,693 --> 00:39:05,093
Aren’t you going to be good again?

584
00:39:09,023 --> 00:39:09,907
No, I’m not.

585
00:39:15,677 --> 00:39:16,406
What are you even saying?

586
00:39:17,068 --> 00:39:17,568
Huh?

587
00:39:19,452 --> 00:39:22,404
Judo is your dream.

588
00:39:24,420 --> 00:39:25,197
Whose dream?

589
00:39:26,124 --> 00:39:27,185
It’s all your idea, Dad.

590
00:39:32,014 --> 00:39:33,955
What’s wrong with you, Niran?

591
00:39:35,740 --> 00:39:38,037
Look how far your friends have gotten.

592
00:39:40,127 --> 00:39:42,080
You’re not going anywhere at this rate.

593
00:39:42,257 --> 00:39:43,397
Do you know that?

594
00:39:43,824 --> 00:39:44,854
Can’t you see that?

595
00:39:46,871 --> 00:39:49,264
Have you ever once asked me
what I wanted?

596
00:39:49,470 --> 00:39:50,949
All you do is say

597
00:39:51,243 --> 00:39:52,863
I’m not good enough, I don’t try.

598
00:39:54,953 --> 00:39:55,661
Why?

599
00:39:57,118 --> 00:39:58,709
If one day I fail,

600
00:39:59,754 --> 00:40:01,415
you’ll leave me like Mom did, right?

601
00:40:03,314 --> 00:40:03,985
Right?

602
00:40:47,214 --> 00:40:47,945
- Hello.
- Oh—

603
00:40:48,195 --> 00:40:49,060
Where’s P’Niran?

604
00:40:50,355 --> 00:40:52,086
He got out of the car
and stormed off somewhere.

605
00:40:53,337 --> 00:40:54,176
Thank you.

606
00:40:54,176 --> 00:40:55,209
Wait.

607
00:41:12,242 --> 00:41:13,059
P’Niran!

608
00:41:27,534 --> 00:41:33,071
♪ Whenever you need me ♪

609
00:41:33,071 --> 00:41:37,783
♪ Just know I’m keeping you in my sight ♪

610
00:41:37,783 --> 00:41:42,314
♪ No matter how dark it might be ♪

611
00:41:42,314 --> 00:41:46,829
♪ Just look up at the sky ♪

612
00:41:46,829 --> 00:41:51,566
♪ I asked every star ♪

613
00:41:51,566 --> 00:41:53,914
♪ To care for you where you are ♪

614
00:41:53,988 --> 00:41:56,481
P’Niran has worked everything out, Nong Cheewa.

615
00:41:56,628 --> 00:41:59,114
Then we can go celebrate now, right?

616
00:41:59,114 --> 00:41:59,665
Hey.

617
00:41:59,797 --> 00:42:00,531
What are you spacing out about?

618
00:42:00,531 --> 00:42:02,295
I’m quitting judo.

619
00:42:02,442 --> 00:42:05,218
Even if there are more things you feel like you’re not good at, that’s okay.

620
00:42:05,218 --> 00:42:07,411
I’ll cheer you on for eternity.

621
00:42:07,411 --> 00:42:08,445
P’Niran, did you know—

622
00:42:08,445 --> 00:42:09,426
P’Niran knows.

623
00:42:09,691 --> 00:42:10,874
He knows you’re worried about him.

624
00:42:11,036 --> 00:42:12,851
P’Niran is so lucky to have you, Cheewa.

625
00:42:13,690 --> 00:42:15,284
Are we boyfriends yet?
